  "analyzed_vuln": {
    "function": "audio_sample_entry_box_read",
    "file": "gpac/src/isomedia/box_code_base.c",
    "description": "`audio_sample_entry_box_read` manually removes and frees `ptr->esd` via `gf_isom_box_del_parent(&ptr->child_boxes, (GF_Box *)ptr->esd)` when scanning malformed QTFF payload for an `esds` box, but it does not clear all ownership aliases before later cleanup. The same `esds` object remains reachable through box ownership state and is freed again during recursive `gf_isom_box_del` / `gf_isom_box_array_del`, producing a heap use-after-free in `gf_isom_box_del` on already-freed box memory.",
    "conditions": "In fuzz_parse, provide an `mp4a` sample entry with malformed/truncated child layout (as in PoC: `mp4a` + `wave` + embedded `esds`) so normal `gf_isom_box_array_read` fails and the fallback scan path in `audio_sample_entry_box_read` executes. If `ptr->esd` was already set from earlier child parsing, the fallback calls `gf_isom_box_del_parent` on it and then reparses/continues; later movie teardown (`gf_isom_close` -> `gf_isom_delete_movie` -> recursive box deletion) traverses stale ownership and touches the freed `esds` again, triggering UAF."
  },
